Honestly, the gory photos would just make me look away. Bowel tumours on a packet of crisps? I'd think it was trying too hard, and I'd still grab whatever's nearest. The plain text warnings are the same as the posters on the bus: I'd read the first line and move on.

The calorie badge is the only bit I'd actually use. I'm watching what things cost, so a number on the front is something I can compare, even if I don't know what a "good" number is. Doing it with the gore on the same pack would just annoy me into ignoring the lot.

