Right, so it's a vending machine with a row of snacks, and I'm meant to be fussy about which ones I pick. Honestly, the fancy pictures would just make me roll my eyes. Bowel tumour on a packet of Doritos? I know what Doritos do. The photos feel like they're trying to frighten a child.

The calorie numbers are more use. If the Dairy Milk says 240 and the fruit pot says 95, that's a comparison I can make in two seconds at the machine, and I might grab the pot, especially on a day I've had four cups of tea and no lunch. Plain text warnings I'd just skim past like the ones on the cigarette packets. And with no labels at all, I'd be buying exactly what I always buy.

